s common lipoprotein delivered as naked DNA or recombinant protein</article-title><source>DNA Cell Biol</source><year>2002</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>107</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11953009</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1089/104454902753604970</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>TF</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirkham</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Lesse</surname><given-names>AJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Construction of a mutant and characterization of the role of the vaccine antigen P6 in outer membrane integrity of nontypeable Haemophilus influenzae</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2006</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>5169</fpage><lpage>5176</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16926409</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/IAI.00692-06</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fortney</surname><given-names>KR</given-names></name><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauer</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Katz</surname><given-names>BP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hood</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name><name><surname>Munson</surname><given-names>RS</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name><name><surname>Spinola</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Expression of peptidoglycan-associated lipoprotein is required for virulence in the human model of Haemophilus ducreyi infection</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><year>2000</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>6441</fpage><lpage>6448</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11035757</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/IAI.68.11.6441-6448.2000</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"